{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Suhemanta","html":"<article id='thag1.106'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.106 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.106 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekādasamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Eleven </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Suhemantattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Suhemanta </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Sataliṅgassa atthassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Though the meaning has a hundred facets, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>satalakkhaṇadhārino; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and bears a hundred characteristics, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ekaṅgadassī dummedho, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the simpleton sees only one factor, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>satadassī ca paṇḍito”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>while the sage sees a hundred. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Suhemanto thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
